hey ask you to analyze them  because they've tested them and there's  a known amount of  compound in there and they want to see  if you also  are able to get the results similar to  theirs  employee training is also tracked under  iso  and they're also looking at in the  training records having tests to  prove that the training was effective  documenting  instrument maintenance repair as well as  calibrations  noting when calibrations are next due  not allowing  testing to be done on an instrument  that's out of calibration  also looking at things such as  preventive and corrected corrective and  preventative actions kappas  the crm module allows clients to keep  track of any complaints against the  laboratory  if any testing was complete and perhaps  a report was missing  a page was missing from a final report  sent to a client  those all need to be tracked analyzed  and  remediated and then finally reporting  reporting to metric reporting to clients  reporting  invoices and then having internal  reports such as work list reports or  management reports backlog production  and then finally electronic data  exchange where you may be working with  other organizations that want to import  those results  into their system we talked a little bit  about metric it's basically a regulatory  compliance system  built by regulators for oversight and it  provides  necessary visibility for adherence to  the rules regulations and statuses  it's both it has both an industry side  as well as a regulatory side  the industry side is used to report  required events and information  while the regulatory side is used for  enforcement and compliance monitoring  so that is something very important for  many states  now we talked about production through  analysis  many laboratories focus on one type of  testing whether it's just a cut like  contract commercial testing where they  receive product  be it you know food products for testing  or  raw material maybe it's just  the powder or the